 ## Overview
-Ray-marched volumetric fog simulates light absorption, scattering, soft shadows, and light shafts (god rays) by treating fog as a 3D volume of participating media traced via forward ray-marching from the camera to the scene [S1, unofficial]. It differs from backward ray-marching by allowing early-out optimizations when transmittance becomes negligible, and it decouples the physical density data from visual appearance rules via material parameterization and gradient-based classification as defined in [Specific Material and Geometry Rendering](4395-specific-material-and-geometry-rendering.md).
